 \\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328130 13194139535037 true] [17592186328129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328131 13194139535037 true] [17592186328129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328132 13194139535037 true] [17592186328129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328133 13194139535037 true] [17592186328129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328134 13194139535037 true] [17592186328129 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535037 true] [17592186328129 1041 "selection" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328129 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328132 13194139535037 true] [17592186328129 1110 #uuid "93d2620f-1f6d-5040-8b0b-4b2ab060a0ac" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328130 1034 "t=\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328130 1111 #uuid "0f07e773-26f2-50c1-91ae-7b5f27852d18" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328131 1034 "t=\\pm \\sqrt{2}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328131 1111 #uuid "6fb41d8e-f957-53e7-b18b-6ee006245371" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328132 1034 "t=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328132 1111 #uuid "42dc512a-ad60-5da4-9b5b-47c0a03ded2d" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328133 1034 "t=\\pm 3\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328133 1111 #uuid "9f33c913-b9a1-58a8-aafd-788c84cf79c2" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328134 1034 "t=\\pm \\sqrt{6}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328134 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328134 1111 #uuid "fc6fe34a-5405-57c7-acd4-bcd7e6f5617d" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328135 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328136 13194139535037 true] [17592186328135 1089 "q-122947" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328135 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535037 true] [17592186328135 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\pi t)-2t,\\,y={e}^{2t},\\,0<t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the value of the parameter $t$ at which the normal line to the curve is horizontal." 13194139535037 true] [17592186328135 1113 #uuid "19efb6b5-9426-572c-bf66-26e959bfbbc7" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328135 1145 "The normal line is horizontal when the tangent line to the curve is vertical. Therefore, we require ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{t}-2,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{2t}\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{t}-2=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})=2{e}^{2\\times (1/2)}=2e\\ne 0,\\,\\,\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed horizontal when $t=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328137 13194139535037 true] [17592186328136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328138 13194139535037 true] [17592186328136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328139 13194139535037 true] [17592186328136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328140 13194139535037 true] [17592186328136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328141 13194139535037 true] [17592186328136 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535037 true] [17592186328136 1041 "selection" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328136 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328138 13194139535037 true] [17592186328136 1110 #uuid "a08bb09e-37be-5694-afb1-667e3550486f" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328137 1034 "t=\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328137 1111 #uuid "8c36bbe9-1359-5618-a74e-edf5d5758e89" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328138 1034 "t=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328138 1111 #uuid "f6b732c1-6425-5d0f-8380-2b4345b44297" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328139 1034 "t=-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328139 1111 #uuid "581c818c-c60b-5513-940f-e72fc8e87637" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328140 1034 "t=-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328140 1111 #uuid "ecc7068d-f209-5dd4-9838-7a2290dccd66" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328141 1034 "t=\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328141 1111 #uuid "799bf862-ae41-5d1c-8d42-b041355736d6" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328142 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328143 13194139535037 true] [17592186328142 1089 "q-15564" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328142 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535037 true] [17592186328142 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{1}{3},\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nLet $C$ be the point that corresponds to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ on the curve. Determine the point at which the tangent to the curve at $C$ crosses the $x$-axis." 13194139535037 true] [17592186328142 1113 #uuid "29f052c6-c270-5aa0-8344-16e349b88fda" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328142 1145 "First, we find the coordinates of the point $C$ by substituting $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ into the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{3}=1+0+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}, \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+1=0+1=1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we're looking to find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at the point $(\\frac{4}{3},1).$ \n\nTo find the equation of the tangent line, we need to find $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$ To compute it, we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the slope of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t=\\pi /2} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-0} \\\\  & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the equation of the tangent line, we use point-slope form with the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(\\frac{4}{3},1)$ and the slope $m=1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-1 & =1\\cdot (x-\\frac{4}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent crosses the $x$-axis when $y=0.$ At this point, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0-1 & =1\\cdot (x-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\ -1 & =x-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $(\\frac{1}{3},\\,0)$ is the $x$-intercept." 13194139535037 true] [17592186328143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328144 13194139535037 true] [17592186328143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328145 13194139535037 true] [17592186328143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328146 13194139535037 true] [17592186328143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328147 13194139535037 true] [17592186328143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328148 13194139535037 true] [17592186328143 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535037 true] [17592186328143 1041 "selection" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328143 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328145 13194139535037 true] [17592186328143 1110 #uuid "7b451a3c-d09b-569f-b68b-2e254be9f79a" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328144 1034 "(\\frac{2}{7},\\,0)" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328144 1111 #uuid "a9be2ac7-5fdd-59a2-b70c-40b4bd4cb786" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328145 1034 "(\\frac{1}{3},\\,0)" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328145 1111 #uuid "bea35c93-97ea-51a9-8061-be15a1b089eb" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328146 1034 "(\\frac{1}{4},\\,0)" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328146 1111 #uuid "d88fd828-b456-5597-85df-f66c9c59d4a5" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328147 1034 "(\\frac{2}{5},\\,0)" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328147 1111 #uuid "07ab2975-6f45-5014-a6d4-2b2d1ef8c422" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328148 1034 "(\\frac{2}{9},\\,0)" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328148 1111 #uuid "95ada701-0cff-52d5-8c80-2c08f142ed3e" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328149 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328150 13194139535037 true] [17592186328149 1089 "q-20853" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328149 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535037 true] [17592186328149 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=2(t+1),\\,y=4{t}^{2},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the value of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal." 13194139535037 true] [17592186328149 1113 #uuid "83179f5c-6e11-5515-9a0e-188d40ccc82d" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328149 1145 "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=8t.\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n8t=0\\,⟹\\,t=0.\n$$\n\nNote that ${x}^{′}(0)=2\\ne 0.$ Therefore, we conclude that when $t=0,$ the tangent to the curve is horizontal." 13194139535037 true] [17592186328150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328151 13194139535037 true] [17592186328150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328152 13194139535037 true] [17592186328150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328153 13194139535037 true] [17592186328150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328154 13194139535037 true] [17592186328150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328155 13194139535037 true] [17592186328150 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535037 true] [17592186328150 1041 "selection" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328150 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328152 13194139535037 true] [17592186328150 1110 #uuid "330f0c30-040a-5b5d-9aac-fb07db5dca33" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328151 1034 "t=1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328151 1111 #uuid "f9ba7e1c-d785-511e-981c-1680eead2835" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328152 1034 "t=0" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328152 1111 #uuid "96f6a909-444e-509b-980d-3db4763ed0d7" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328153 1034 "t=-1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328153 1111 #uuid "106961b3-6b50-5e77-970c-ade213532dbf" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328154 1034 "t=-2" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328154 1111 #uuid "96c75a6f-41fb-5252-b22e-e925b86d7ca1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328155 1034 "t=3" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328155 1111 #uuid "465faa5f-21c0-5624-bcbc-15c6e69eb750" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328156 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328157 13194139535037 true] [17592186328156 1089 "q-348109" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328156 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535037 true] [17592186328156 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx={t}^{3}-4t,\\,y=2{t}^{2}+1,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nFind the Cartesian equation of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=2.$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the tangent line is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535037 true] [17592186328156 1113 #uuid "c84a1a58-ffd9-56ee-a3b8-04aed5e73d9c" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328156 1145 "First, we find the coordinates of the point by substituting $t=2$ into the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(2)^{3}-4(2)=8-8=0 \\\\ y & =2(2)^{2}+1=2(4)+1=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we're looking to find the equation of the tangent at the point $(0,9).$ \n\nTo find the equation of the tangent line, we need to find $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$ To compute it, we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}-4,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=4t\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4t}{3{t}^{2}-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=2,$ the slope of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t\\,=\\,2} & =\\frac{4(2)}{3(2)^{2}-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3(4)-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{12-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{8} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the Cartesian equation of the tangent line, we use point-slope form with the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,9)$ and the slope $m=1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-9 & =1(x-0) \\\\ y-9 & =x \\\\ y & =x+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the equation of the tangent line  in slope-intercept form is $y=x+9.$" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328157 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328158 13194139535037 true] [17592186328157 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535037 true] [17592186328157 1041 "field-1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328157 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328158 13194139535037 true] [17592186328157 1110 #uuid "f83e753d-01f2-5c37-8053-3beebf304df1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328158 1034 "x+9" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328158 1111 #uuid "40cdb695-341c-5869-a750-a6eeeed896cf" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328159 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328160 13194139535037 true] [17592186328159 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328162 13194139535037 true] [17592186328159 1089 "q-348115" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328159 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535037 true] [17592186328159 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=t(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2),\\,y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,t\\in (0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nLet $C$ be the point that corresponds to $t=e$ on the curve. Determine the coordinates of the point at which the tangent to the curve at $C$ crosses the $y$-axis. Do not round the answers.\n\nThe tangent to the curve at $C$ crosses the $y$-axis at $(${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328159 1113 #uuid "917cc07e-7c6c-5b76-ae6f-472870182042" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328159 1145 "First, we find the coordinates of the point $C$ by substituting $t=e$ into the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =e(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+2)=3e \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡e=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we're looking to find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at the point $(3e,1).$ \n\nTo find the equation of the tangent line, we need to find $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$ To compute it, we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+3,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{t}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=e,$ the slope of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t\\,=\\,e} & =\\frac{1}{e(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the equation of the tangent line, we use point-slope form with the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3e,1)$ and the slope $m=\\frac{1}{4e}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-1=\\frac{1}{4e}(x-3e).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent crosses the $y$-axis when $x=0.$ At this point, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-1 & =\\frac{1}{4e}(0-3e) \\\\ y-1 & =-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the tangent to the curve at $C$ crosses the $y$-axis at $(0,\\,\\frac{1}{4}).$" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328161 13194139535037 true] [17592186328160 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535037 true] [17592186328160 1041 "field-1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328160 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328161 13194139535037 true] [17592186328160 1110 #uuid "a7d2e78c-13f9-5dcf-9b01-be7664af1dcb" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328161 1034 "0" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328161 1111 #uuid "fb9ffbbc-82f7-5087-a26e-121a53e06471" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328162 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328163 13194139535037 true] [17592186328162 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535037 true] [17592186328162 1041 "field-2" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328162 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328163 13194139535037 true] [17592186328162 1110 #uuid "8eba9c9c-e598-56dc-9a36-2a764a59a1ae" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328163 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328163 1111 #uuid "43e70bd0-e92a-5815-844f-5acaf51122a9" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328164 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328165 13194139535037 true] [17592186328164 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328167 13194139535037 true] [17592186328164 1089 "q-350359" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328164 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535037 true] [17592186328164 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}t+\\frac{1}{2},\\,y={t}^{3}+7{t}^{2}+8t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Do not round the answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139535037 true] [17592186328164 1113 #uuid "5e73fc07-6c36-55be-b36c-099a85861c24" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328164 1145 "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2t+\\frac{1}{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}+14t+8\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+14t+8 & =0 \\\\ (3t+2)(t+4) & =0 \\\\ t & =-4,-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(-4) & =2(-4)+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{15}{2}\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(-\\frac{2}{3}) & =2(-\\frac{2}{3})+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{5}{6}\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal at $t=-4$ and $t=-\\frac{2}{3}.$" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328166 13194139535037 true] [17592186328165 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535037 true] [17592186328165 1041 "field-1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328165 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328166 13194139535037 true] [17592186328165 1110 #uuid "a81fd662-a2da-5909-9235-44ffc4e05fc7" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328166 1034 "-4" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328166 1111 #uuid "616cf01b-42d0-5398-9319-1677eaae1af2" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328168 13194139535037 true] [17592186328167 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535037 true] [17592186328167 1041 "field-2" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328167 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328168 13194139535037 true] [17592186328167 1110 #uuid "4c669d61-c30a-5583-b15c-acdfb974c3fe" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328168 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328168 1111 #uuid "ee186c82-2942-5353-9be7-a213161b973f" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328169 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328170 13194139535037 true] [17592186328169 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328172 13194139535037 true] [17592186328169 1089 "q-350368" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328169 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535037 true] [17592186328169 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx={e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t),\\,y={e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t),\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Do not round the answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139535037 true] [17592186328169 1113 #uuid "87619e0a-4cfe-5be8-a034-9a2f3a043e1c" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328169 1145 "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)),\\,{y}^{′}(t)={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)} & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)=-1 \\\\ t & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & ={e}^{\\frac{3\\pi }{4}}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})]=-\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\frac{3\\pi }{4}}\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) & ={e}^{\\frac{7\\pi }{4}}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})]=\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\frac{7\\pi }{4}}\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal at $t=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $t=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.$" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328171 13194139535037 true] [17592186328170 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535037 true] [17592186328170 1041 "field-1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328170 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328171 13194139535037 true] [17592186328170 1110 #uuid "91466fa3-7d86-54a5-b315-bd73faedc724" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328171 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi}{4}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328171 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328171 1111 #uuid "e2eaef25-fa40-5474-aa93-94d7dc5679c9" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328173 13194139535037 true] [17592186328172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535037 true] [17592186328172 1041 "field-2" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328172 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328173 13194139535037 true] [17592186328172 1110 #uuid "cca0e8a3-bd4a-513a-a193-de1493cad4eb" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328173 1034 "\\frac{7\\pi}{4}" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328173 1111 #uuid "307d88f7-62e2-560a-8ec2-6717b4a2e408" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328174 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328175 13194139535037 true] [17592186328174 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328177 13194139535037 true] [17592186328174 1089 "q-350386" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328174 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535037 true] [17592186328174 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}t+\\frac{1}{2},\\,y={t}^{3}+7{t}^{2}+8t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nLet $C$ be the point that corresponds to $t=-1$ on the curve. Determine the coordinates of the point at which the normal to the curve at $C$ crosses the $x$-axis. Do not round the answers.\n\nThe normal to the curve at $C$ crosses the $x$-axis at $(${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328174 1113 #uuid "69d258b7-b3e5-504c-8494-6e597182b1b1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328174 1145 "First, we find the coordinates of the point $C$ by substituting $t=-1$ into the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(-1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(-1)+\\frac{1}{2}=1-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1 \\\\ y & =(-1)^{3}+7(-1)^{2}+8(-1)=-1+7-8=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we're looking to determine the equation of the normal at the point $(1,-2).$ For this, we need to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ which means we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2t+\\frac{1}{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}+14t+8\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{t}^{2}+14t+8}{2t+\\frac{1}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=-1,$ the slope of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t\\,=\\,-1} & =\\frac{3(-1)^{2}+14(-1)+8}{2(-1)+\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{(-\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope ${m}_{n}$ of the normal line, we take the negative reciprocal of $m:$\n\n$$\n{m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the equation of the normal, we use point-slope form with the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(1,-2)$ and the slope ${m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(-2) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) \\\\ y+2 & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal intersects the $x$-axis when $y=0.$ At this point, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+2 & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) & =2 \\\\ x-1 & =-4 \\\\ x & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the normal to the curve at $C$ crosses the $x$-axis at $(-3,\\,0).$" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328175 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328176 13194139535037 true] [17592186328175 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535037 true] [17592186328175 1041 "field-1" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328175 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328176 13194139535037 true] [17592186328175 1110 #uuid "c3d2dd08-1509-5e0c-9b20-97122d754d7e" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328176 1034 "-3" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535037 true] [17592186328176 1111 #uuid "0e5635d8-8141-5a78-909f-d5cf0dfa92d8" 13194139535037 true] [17592186328177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328178 13194139535037 true] [17592186328177 1040 #edb/re